cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "petri, a falsifiable test bench for connectome to behavior hypotheses in caenorhabditis elegans"
title: "petri"
authors:
  - alias: esnond
version: 1.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER-FILL-AT-RELEASE
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/esnond/petri"
abstract: >-
  a whole animal simulator of caenorhabditis elegans locomotion in c99.
  graded neuron dynamics on published connectome reconstructions
  (wormatlas white 1986 series, openworm hermaphrodite edge list,
  witvliet 2021 developmental volumes), a 24 segment hydrostatic body
  with quasi static anisotropic friction, proprioceptive wave
  generation, single neuron ablation screening and genome evolution.
  deterministic per seed, zero dependencies beyond libc and libm.
keywords:
  - caenorhabditis elegans
  - connectome
  - locomotion
  - neuromechanics
  - falsifiability